course: dictionary
lesson: 9769
title: Surely: certain, and steady
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Surely means for certain, with no doubt. «Here, in this holy place, here if anywhere, surely we shall find Him!» The Rat is so sure they will find the god that he says it with no doubt at all.
explain: Surely is also used when you think something must be true and are a little surprised it might not be. «Surely you know that!» The speaker thinks you ought to know it already. Swap in certainly or definitely: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the meaning.
explain: Surely also sits in phrases. Slowly but surely means slowly but steadily, like a tortoise who never stops. In a maths puzzle, surely means in every case, even the worst one: how many socks must you pick from a dark drawer to surely get a matching pair?
fact: Surely means for certain, with no doubt.
fact: Surely can show strong belief, as in «Surely you can do it!»
fact: In a maths puzzle, surely means in every case, even the worst one.
fact: Slowly but surely means slowly but steadily.
fact: Pevno is a Czech word that means surely or of course, a strong agreement.
exercise: The Rat says «surely we shall find Him!» What does surely mean here? | Quickly and in a hurry | *For certain, with no doubt | Maybe, if we are lucky | Never
exercise: What does the phrase slowly but surely mean? | Very fast and loud | *Slowly but steadily | Quietly, in a whisper | Not at all
exercise: Which word shows strong belief in «Surely you can do it!»? | Do | *Surely | It | Can
test: In a maths puzzle, «How many must you pick to surely get two of a kind?» What does surely mean? | Only if you are very lucky | Without counting | *In every case, even the worst one | Maybe you will get them
test: Which sentence uses surely to show the speaker thinks you should already know something? | Let us go to the park. | Pass the bread, please. | *Surely you know that! | The cat sat on the mat.
exam: In «Surely we shall find Him!», which meaning fits best? | Slowly and quietly | *For certain, with no doubt | Angrily | Perhaps, or it might happen
